#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-copy-from-dom0.rst:65
#: f8ff6d87df5a4a369c26d9dfd5111645
msgid "Copying *to* dom0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-copy-from-dom0.rst:68
#: 94c0c16db9144707964c387cb350b54b
msgid ""
"Copying anything into dom0 is not advised, since doing so can compromise the "
"security of your Qubes system. For this reason, there is no simple means of "
"copying anything into dom0, unlike :ref:`user/how-to-guides/how-to-copy-from-"
"dom0:copying *from* dom0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-copy-from-dom0.rst:70
#: de5d5a6df9ec40a081b4d8901fe05eff
msgid ""
"There should normally be few reasons for the user to want to copy anything "
"from domUs to dom0, as dom0 only acts as a “thin trusted terminal”, and no "
"user applications run there. Sometimes, new users feel the urge to copy a "
"desktop wallpaper image into dom0, but that is not necessary. A safer "
"approach is simply to display the image in :doc:`full-screen mode </user/how-"
"to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode>` in an app qube, then take a "
"screenshot from dom0, which results in exactly the image needed for a "
"wallpaper, created securely and natively in dom0."
msgstr ""

